{
  "target": "src.api.report_view:ReportView",
  "diagnosis": "The class exhibits low cohesion (LCOM4=2) because its methods operate on two distinct clusters of attributes: one cluster uses `_width` for formatting (`title`, `describe_customer`), while the other cluster uses `_repository` and `_mailer` for data retrieval and communication (`order_count`, `mail_summary`). Additionally, `describe_customer` demonstrates feature envy by accessing four attributes of the `Customer` object rather than its own state, suggesting a responsibility mismatch.",
  "suggestions": [
